Z||000032||EdsB52||10-16-2001||02:16 PM||||I think it would be a mistake to kill Bin Laden. He deserves a million horrid deaths, but what is our objective here? To end terrorism. A popular critique of death penalty opponents is that it doesn't create an atmosphere of deterrence. Timothy McVeigh has been virtually forgotten and carries no deterrence value, but how about Charles Manson? He's alive with no chance of freedom; people can feel what he's going through and watch his actions as his brain is obviously deteriorating. Again, I don't subscribe to deterrence theory, but every death penalty advocate I've spoken with does subscribe to it and should therefore apply it to all death penalty matters. Death would be too quick and easy for Bin Laden; life in prison for years before his inevitable execution would be horrible. Just think, he would be surrounded by thousands of born-again Christians. He would be a celebrity to few, but hated and spit on by many. He would rather be killed than shuttled around from court appearance to court appearance with the cameras trained on him. <P>I agree, if captured alive, he will receive full due process including an objective jury of his peers!!! Not Constitutionally guaranteed, but the US judicial system doesn't know how else to operate. I don't believe there are rule for diminished due process. Like it matters anyway! Could set a record for deliberation time. I as well believe the trial should be televised. I think it will and will lend to closure for all Americans, especially those who lost family and friends.||||reg||1
Z||000033||Formula||10-16-2001||03:00 PM||||you know, we could reopen a cell in alcatraz for him.  ||||reg||1
Z||000034||Ken Wittlief||10-16-2001||04:50 PM||||televise his capture and trail and we will literally have terrorist crawling out of the woodwork - every idiot that can get his hands on a gernade or shotgun will be raging a personal jihad in our malls, schools and city streets.<P> This is not crime we are dealing with - there is no deterrent to people that want to die in a holy war.<P> These type of people need to be treated like cancer - kill it as soon as you see it, incenerate the carcass and spread the ashes where they cant be found.<P> No discussion - no media - no victory dance - do everything you can to make it as if he never existed - and prevent anyone else from following in his footsteps.||||reg||10
Z||000035||EdsB52||10-16-2001||07:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR>[B][/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"televise his capture and trail and we will literally have terrorist crawling out of the woodwork - every idiot that can get his hands on a gernade or shotgun will be raging a personal jihad in our malls, schools and city streets."<P>I disagree. Besides, if there are idiots in America that are prone to do this (which there probably are), then they're going to do it anyway, they're just looking/waiting for an excuse. It wouldn't be like the LA riots where the cops were unjustly absolved of beating a black man half to death.<P>"This is not crime we are dealing with - there is no deterrent to people that want to die in a holy war."<P>Well then what is it Ken? Terrorist acts against an entire country aren't crime? I think what you meant to say was this is not conventional crime that we are dealing with. Either way, this is crime and the perpetrators are criminals. You're right, there is no deterrent for crazies that are wiling to die in a holy war. While writing that, you've agreed with my refutation of death penalty advocate's theories that believe the death penalty creates deterrence. It's not logical to believe deterrence works within the US to dissuade monsters from committing premeditated, heinous murder, while having no dissuasive effect on monsters outside the US; they come from the same seed. However, many people will buy into that fallacy to perpetuate the death penalty as a guise for retaliation. I agree that trying and executing the responsible terrorists will have no deterrent value, but that proponents of the death penalty should rethink their rationale for the death penalty in the US. I think it would be fun to parade that SOB around like our capture as a moniker of our defeat of terrorism, while we continue to seek out the rest of the garbage over there.<P>"These type of people need to be treated like cancer - kill it as soon as you see it, incenerate the carcass and spread the ashes where they cant be found."<P>A definite degree of truth to that, and if it goes down that way I'll cheer. I just think it would be fun to parade him around and it would be judicial torture to be held to a US standard for which he hates.<P>"No discussion - no media - no victory dance - do everything you can to make it as if he never existed - and prevent anyone else from following in his footsteps."<P>We can still do the latter with or without the former.||||reg||1
Z||000036||Mach10||10-16-2001||07:47 PM||||Not feeling so well, so i don't feel up to making a nice long post... Goddamn flu, and I have a test tommorrow. this is NOt a good week. Oh, and I have a shift key that works only intermittently. Excuse the capitalization  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>-for the fanatics, there's no changing the way they think or feel. putting UBL on trial would be for the benefit of everyone else. Again, in international politics, appearance is everything. most of the world is somewhat skeptical of the US's 'evidence' against ubl. A public trial will bring this to light.<P>-good point was raised. We aren't at war with Afghanistan, and I think people should try and remember that. The US declared war against the Taliban extremist movement, a political/militant party whose legitimacy is only acknowledged by Pakistan. therefore, Afghani civilian casualties are a little more serious than 'collateral damage'<BR>But i'm not blaming the US. So far they are doing a pretty good job.<P>- The people protesting around the world are being fed lies and propaganda by their respective spiritual leaders. 99% of them have no idea what's going on, other than "their hero is being unjustly blamed for an accident in the US, and the Big Bad wolf is killing muslims" Assuming that's the only information you've ever recieved, can you blame them for being pissed? Information is very restricted. i bet you that most of the people there don't even know what the world trade center WAS, let alone how many people were killed. Propaganda is very dangerous. <P>I think I'm going to throw up, so you'll excuse me if I stop here. I'll answer back when I feel a little better  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000037||Ken Wittlief||10-17-2001||08:56 AM||||People like OBL WANT public attention - they want to be in the spot light - they WANT everyone to see their face on CNN.<BR> <BR> If we catch him and put him on trial do you think he will be sulking around with his head hung in shame and embarrasment?!<P> He will be ranting and raving the same old thing right up to the second they inject the lethal drug into his iv.<P> and the terrorist acts will flare up again.<P> We need to change the subject. We need to focus on rebuilding afganistan, putting and end to the conflict between pakistand and india, and show the islamic world that we are not out to destroy islam - that america is founded on the principles of freedom, democracy, and personal responsibility.<P> Finding a way for Israel to rebuild their temple, without having to tear down the dome of the rock, would be sign of goodwill on our part, and would resolve some of the tension between the muslims and the jews - both can co-exist in the same area - one does not have to give up anything for the other to have what is important too.<P> We need to get into the terrorists head and difuse their anger without giving them what they want, (our destruction and the destruction of Israel) - If we can make it clear to the islamic people that we are NOT against them, and we are NOT conducting a crusade, then what will they be angry about?<P> Sure you might still have a few nut cases left who wont accept it, but the majority of the muslims will come around and oppose the extreemist "Why do you hate america so?! they are our friends!"||||reg||10
